\mathcal N\">\\(\\mathcal N\\)</span> is the commutant of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal A\">\\(\\mathcal A\\)</span> on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal H\">\\(\\mathcal H\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2ad624e4e75f394b\" href=\"?note=2ad624e4e75f394b\" title=\"58-df-commutant\">58-df-commutant</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}commutant}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{VonNeumannAlgebra}_S(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal H)\\to\n\\exists\\mathcal N_1,\\mathcal N_2\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Commutant}_S(\\mathcal N_1,\\mathcal M,\\mathcal H)\n\\land\\mathrm{Commutant}_S(\\mathcal N_2,\\mathcal N_1,\\mathcal H)\n\\land\\mathcal N_2=\\mathcal M\n\\bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}commutant}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{VonNeumannAlgebra}_S(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal H)\\to\n\\exists\\mathcal N_1,\\mathcal N_2\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Commutant}_S(\\mathcal N_1,\\mathcal M,\\mathcal H)\n\\land\\mathrm{Commutant}_S(\\mathcal N_2,\\mathcal N_1,\\mathcal H)\n\\land\\mathcal N_2=\\mathcal M\n\\bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the typed bicommutant equation already witnessed by the registered von Neumann algebra predicate; the unbound prime notation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal M&#39;&#39;\">\\(\\mathcal M&#39;&#39;\\)</span> is avoided.</li>\n<li><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"2ad624e4e75f394b\" href=\"?note=2ad624e4e75f394b\" title=\"58-df-commutant\">58-df-commutant</a> defines the commutant, not the commutator.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-co